  "note": "INCONCLUSIVE under Test Card T023 (approved c2c4e9413). Bats spend clearly more energy per gram over a lifetime than other mammals (the first condition is met), but less than birds: Delta's interval reaches -0.275, just outside the +-0.25 band, and excludes zero. Flight accounts for about 60 percent of the bird offset; the remainder is not explained by flight, even though bat torpor biases the bat value upward. Not blind (bat longevity known in biology); no phylogenetic correction. Nearest theory: disposable soma and the extrinsic-mortality theory of ageing; not UET-distinct. L2 approved by the author on 2026-11-18."
